# Prose about JCL. Talisman reads the DISP keyword PASS as a password-like
# token, plus ALTERNATE KEY, RPAREN and errors="replace" — twelve low-severity
# false positives, no credential. Checksummed rather than detector-ignored, so
# editing this living ledger re-runs the scan (and needs a fresh checksum).
- filename: docs/corpus-onboarding-blockers.md
  checksum: 2189d70c1754f3fed4282b87abc826275f0aa6a8c2688538ddadd47dcb2e0c42
# The DISP fix. Same false positive as the ledger above: talisman reads the JCL
# disposition keyword PASS as a password-like token, so every assertion naming a
# DISP subparameter trips it. Checksummed, not detector-ignored, so a future edit
# to any of the three re-runs the scan.
- filename: tests/jackal/test_bridge_parser.py
  checksum: cf74463907bafeba9a4bbc397b09a21ab8b955d40a4198d992bdc32ef6d53167
- filename: jcl-bridge/src/test/java/org/jackal/jcl/JclSerializerTest.java
  checksum: 5a396c78efaa9bce2aca84d3a4fd3cf894c839ea9868362fe89e97b9fc7c32c0
- filename: jcl-bridge/src/main/java/org/jackal/jcl/JclSerializer.java
  checksum: 3d9bf96297b80850cfb0a5e4756e8af02e4624c6ffc790698c465b7f1b3bd436
# A submodule pointer's whole content is the 40-hex commit SHA it pins, which
# talisman reads as hex-encoded text (and whose gitlink mode it cannot stat at
# all: "error parsing filesize ... submodule"). No checksum here on purpose —
# one would go stale on every pin bump.
- filename: proleap-bridge/proleap-cobol-parser
  ignore_detectors:
    - filecontent
version: "1.0"
